This regression keeps two nested namespace definitions open across the
application header boundary. The header owns both namespace introducers and
opening braces; the including source owns both closing braces.

The transformed variable forces AST-based header emission. The generated
header and source must therefore consume the namespace's explicit source
fragments without synthesizing closes in the header or inferring the source
closes from cross-file declaration ranges. The nested case also requires
close-only unparsing to traverse the inner namespace before emitting the outer
close. The final syntax-only compile checks the two generated files together.
